comdlg32: give a wrapped custom-control label the height its lines need (InDesign Save As / Export)

InDesign 2026's Save As clipped its "Always Save Preview Images with Documents" check box onto two
cut lines, and its Export dialog showed only the middle line ("Name as the Output") of "Use
InDesign Document Name as the Output Filename". The Common Item Dialog gives every
IFileDialogCustomize control a fixed width (160 px at 96 dpi); a longer label wraps, but
ctrl_resize computed the height from the number of '\n' in it ("FIXME: line-wrap"), so the wrapped
lines had no room.

ctrl_resize now measures the label with DrawText(DT_CALCRECT|DT_WORDBREAK) in the room the control
gives its text (for a check or radio button, beside its box as user32's button paints it: 12 px *
dpi / 96 + 1, then half a '0') and takes the larger of that and the old height. A label that fits
keeps the height it had; widths and the column layout are unchanged.

Harness preserved-fixes/harnesses/fd-checkbox.c (IFileDialogCustomize Save dialog with InDesign's
label, a short one and a push button): 11.10-137 FAILS (needs 46 px tall, control 31), patched
PASSES (control 54; the short label stays 31). InDesign 2026: Save As shows both lines; Export
shows all three; Place's check boxes unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
@@ -1011,24 +1011,47 @@
     font = (HFONT)SendMessageW(hctrl, WM_GETFONT, 0, 0);
     font = SelectObject(hdc, font);
     GetTextExtentPoint32W(hdc, text, lstrlenW(text), &size);
-    SelectObject(hdc, font);
-    ReleaseDC(hctrl, hdc);
+
+    final_width = min(max(size.cx, min_width) + 4, max_width);
 
     if(len && multiline)
     {
-        /* FIXME: line-wrap */
+        /* NEUTRON: a label wider than its control wraps, so measure the lines it wraps to in the room the
+         * control gives its text, instead of counting only the '\n' in it ("FIXME: line-wrap" upstream). A
+         * check or radio button paints its text beside its box (user32 button.c: 12 px * dpi / 96 + 1, then
+         * half a '0'). InDesign's Save As "Always Save Preview Images with Documents" wrapped onto a second
+         * line that the control had no height for. A label that fits keeps the height it had. */
+        RECT text_rc;
+        UINT room = final_width;
+        LONG style = GetWindowLongW(hctrl, GWL_STYLE) & BS_TYPEMASK;
+        WCHAR cls[16];
+
+        GetClassNameW(hctrl, cls, ARRAY_SIZE(cls));
+        if(!wcsicmp(cls, L"Button") &&
+           (style == BS_CHECKBOX || style == BS_AUTOCHECKBOX || style == BS_3STATE || style == BS_AUTO3STATE ||
+            style == BS_RADIOBUTTON || style == BS_AUTORADIOBUTTON))
+        {
+            INT zero;
+            GetCharWidthW(hdc, '0', '0', &zero);
+            room -= min(room, 12 * GetDpiForWindow(hctrl) / 96 + 1 + zero / 2);
+        }
+        SetRect(&text_rc, 0, 0, room, 0);
+        DrawTextW(hdc, text, -1, &text_rc, DT_CALCRECT | DT_WORDBREAK);
+
+        /* as before for a label that does not wrap */
         for(lines = 1, c = text; *c != '\0'; c++)
             if(*c == '\n') lines++;
 
-        final_height = size.cy*lines + 2*4;
+        final_height = max(size.cy*lines, text_rc.bottom) + 2*4;
     }
     else
     {
         GetWindowRect(hctrl, &rc);
         final_height = rc.bottom - rc.top;
     }
+    SelectObject(hdc, font);
+    ReleaseDC(hctrl, hdc);
 
-    final_width = min(max(size.cx, min_width) + 4, max_width);
     SetWindowPos(hctrl, NULL, 0, 0, final_width, final_height,
                  SWP_NOZORDER | SWP_NOMOVE | SWP_NOACTIVATE);
 
